  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   ; the run turns so the next temp is written to the same
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                                ; address
                                                               ; ROTATE FORTY BY FOUR  DOWNWARD  entered at the first
                                                               ; byte of a forty byte run with four free cells
                                                               ; immediately below it; every byte moves down four
                                                               ; places and the first four wrap round to the top; the
                                                               ; pointer comes back where it started;
;
                                                               ; THIS IS THE CONVEYOR AT THE SIZE THE TEMP RUN WANTS;
                                                               ; aes/decrypt128 stores ten four byte schedule temps
                                                               ; and must write each one to a FIXED address  so the
                                                               ; run turns under the write point instead of the write
                                                               ; point moving along the run; An include takes no
                                                               ; parameters  so the upward turn is a separate file:
                                                               ; block/rotate40up4;
;
                                                               ; MEASURED AT 122 THOUSAND 524 INSTRUCTIONS A TURN on
                                                               ; random bytes  against the 138 million of one
                                                               ; decrypted block; Nineteen turns  ten storing and nine
                                                               ; reading  come to 2 million 328 thousand: one point
                                                               ; seven percent; The alternative was turning the whole
                                                               ; 176 byte schedule at 1 million 300 thousand a turn
                                                               ; and HANDOFF carries both measurements; every byte
                                                               ; moves down four places  the lowest four into the
                                                               ; scratch
